# g55-fu-engine: core wire lines

1. Apply native/core/crates/mixdog-app-protocol/pending-rows/g55-fu-engine.rows (the new host request host/browser/upload/receiver with its
   free_text row, BrowserPageReadOptions.attributes and .limit, HostBrowserEmulationResult.labels), regenerate the goldens, schema files and
   packages/protocol/src/index.ts, then delete the rows file. mixdog-browser-engine (port.rs upload_receiver, actions/upload.rs, observe.rs,
   emulation.rs, flow.rs, settle/reply_wait.rs) does not compile before this.
2. No Cargo, compose_flip.rs or SERVICE_PENDING line: the new method is a host request (served by the desktop), not a core service method.
3. s4-core-events-service (browser_engine_service.rs): the wiring lines of deferred-g5.md stay as written for CORE-WIRE-G7. The two review
   notes (host_gone only on the newer desktop's first push or the earlier connection's close, not at claim time; a claimant that closes before
   it pushes anything never triggers it) need the single ClaimHook the system proxy already holds: decide there when composing the lane.
